// Title: Communication To Ngrok Tunneling Service - Linux
// Sigma ID: 19bf6fdb-7721-4f3d-867f-53467f6a5db6
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-11-03 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: exfiltration, command-and-control, T1567, T1568.002, T1572, T1090, T1102, S0508
// Description: Detects an executable accessing an ngrok tunneling endpoint, which could be a sign of forbidden
//   exfiltration of data exfiltration by malicious actors
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate use of ngrok
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/hakluke/status/1587733971814977537/photo/1
//   - https://ngrok.com/docs/gateway/agent/ssh-reverse-tunnel-agent
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/linux/network_connection/net_connection_lnx_ngrok_tunnel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.us.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.eu.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.ap.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.au.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.sa.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.jp.ngrok.com" or RemoteUrl contains "tunnel.in.ngrok.com"
